&lt;p&gt;It defaults to Moonshot AI&amp;rsquo;s Kimi models, which are known for strong coding and long context, and can also connect to other compatible providers. Features include built-in subagents for coding, exploring, and planning, support for the Model Context Protocol to connect tools, lifecycle hooks for automation and safety checks, and an ACP mode so editors like Zed and JetBrains can drive it.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>